/target
.smith/
.claude/worktrees/

# graphify writes a knowledge graph under graphify-out/. Two of those files are
# worth keeping and the rest are not, so the ignore list is explicit rather
# than a blanket directory.
#
# Kept: GRAPH_REPORT.md, because it is prose a human reads, and
# .graphify_labels.json, because the community names in it were written by a
# person and survive a rebuild.
#
# Ignored below, for three different reasons:
#
#  - graph.json / graph.html / cache/ are derived data, regenerated wholesale
#    on every run. Committing them adds ~14 MB to history *per rebuild*, and
#    nothing regenerates them on a merge, so they go stale silently — a graph
#    that confidently answers about code that has since moved is worse than no
#    graph. Rebuild with `/graphify --update`, which re-extracts only the files
#    that changed.
#  - manifest.json and cost.json are per-machine bookkeeping (incremental-update
#    state and a token-spend log).
#  - .graphify_python and .graphify_root hold absolute paths into whoever ran it
#    last ("/home/<user>/.local/share/uv/tools/..."). The skill *reads*
#    .graphify_python to pick an interpreter, so a committed one is not merely
#    noise: it points a teammate's run at a path that does not exist.
graphify-out/graph.json
graphify-out/graph.html
graphify-out/cache/
graphify-out/manifest.json
graphify-out/cost.json
graphify-out/.graphify_python
graphify-out/.graphify_root
